<title>JAPAN: Japan construction sector firms rebound.</title>
<headline>Japan construction sector firms rebound.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Firms in Japan's construction sector rebounded in the Monday morning session, as investors considered them oversold, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0153 GMT, Taisei Corp shares were up eight yen at 641 yen. Obayashi Corp was up five yen at 860 yen. Kajima Corp rose four yen to 914 yen.  </p>
<p>&quot;The loss-cutting phase seems to be over for the time being,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
<p>He added that the rise stemmed mostly from technical reasons and had little to do with the recent market trend to buy global issues.</p>
